Probably not. :-)

> /etc/sysconfig/network is:
> 
> NETWORKING=YES
> FORWARD_IPV4=NO
> HOSTNAME=localhost.localdomain
                   ^^^^^^
              Hm, I would put something here; even if only for
              an "internal" use. 

> GATEWAYDEV=
> GATEWAY=
> 
> /etc/rc.d/rc.sysinit includes the lines:
> 
> if [ -f /etc/sysconfig/network ]; then
> 	. /etc/sysconfig/network
> 
> else
> 	NETWORKING=no
